   "text": {
    "L1": "Louis Braille hurt his eye when he was three years old.",
    "L2": "He went to a school for the blind, and made a six-dot system by fifteen.",
    "L3": "Braille uses raised dots. People read them by touching with their fingertips.",
    "L4": "Louis was determined because he worked on his code for three years and did not give up.",
    "L5": "He invented Braille. Invented means he made something new, not that he discovered something already there.",
    "L6": "Use was for one person and were for more than one. Use for with a length of time, such as for three years.",
    "L7": "Now put the three events in the order they happened."
   },
